url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevologic/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"# FROZEN-42 D follow-up — restore the missing Q1 9:46 Kelce TD before 14-0 in the current 11-26 edition (data-only)\n\nDraft PR to `develop`. **This is the FROZEN-42 D follow-up.** It is a separate data-only PR from #421 and does not change that branch or those files.\n\n**This changes the current homepage edition.** `data/narrative.json` is the live current edition and is byte-identical to `data/narrative_editions/2026-11-26-0948.json`. Both files receive the same raw-text insertion and remain byte-identical to each other.\n\nThe 11-26 lede is unchanged (it already opens with the final 34-7, which Karen called fine). The hole is only in `$.lastGameReview.takeaways[0].body`, which jumped to “His 3-yard score up the middle at Q1 0:48 made it 14-0” without the first score.\n\nInserted sentence (ESPN 401873067 `scoringPlays[0]`): `Patrick Mahomes found Travis Kelce for an 8-yard touchdown at Q1 9:46 to make it 7-0.`\n\nOne commit, two paths, no re-serialize, trailing newlines kept, no asset or sitemap changes, no code or generator changes. This PR does not merge or undraft itself.\n\n## L1\n\nExactly two files, same bytes:\n\n- `data/narrative.json`\n- `data/narrative_editions/2026-11-26-0948.json`\n\nRecursive compare of parsed JSON: **only** `$.lastGameReview.takeaways[0].body` changed in each file. Stripping the inserted sentence from the head bytes recovers the develop base byte-for-byte in both files. The inserted sentence appears exactly once per file.\n\n## L2\n\n`$.lastGameReview.takeaways[0].body`\n\nBefore:\n\n> Emmett Johnson had 23 carries for 105 yards and a touchdown, plus four catches, 27 touches. His 3-yard score up the middle at Q1 0:48 made it 14-0.\n\nAfter:\n\n> Emmett Johnson had 23 carries for 105 yards and a touchdown, plus four catches, 27 touches. Patrick Mahomes found Travis Kelce for an 8-yard touchdown at Q1 9:46 to make it 7-0. His 3-yard score up the middle at Q1 0:48 made it 14-0.\n\n## L6\n\nExact-head attempt 1. The first executed attempt is the receipt. An `action_required` attempt with 0 jobs does not count. Head should be 0 behind `develop`.\n\n## Relation to #421\n\n#421 fixed the 11-25 lede and the 11-24 `analysis[0]` hole (FROZEN-42 A and B). This PR is only D, which was disclosed there as a same-class hit deferred so today’s 11-26 edition could stay unchanged until this follow-up.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-26T19:18:54Z","updated_at":"2026-11-26T20:05:49Z","closed_at":"2026-11-26T20:05:49Z","merged_at":"2026-11-26T20:05:49Z","merge_commit_sha":"3a220bd2353d4beaacb6fe03b6d2aaf8e7623fdf","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"stevologic:fix/paesano-1126-takeaway-hole","ref":"fix/paesano-1126-takeaway-hole","repo":{"id":1246237612,"node_id":"R_kgDOSkgTrA","name":"arrowheadpaesanowebsite","full_name":"stevologic/arrowheadpaesanowebsite","owner":{"login":"stevologic","id":5211665,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMTE2NjU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5211665?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevologic","html_url":"https://github.com/stevologic","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevologic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevologic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevologic/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevologic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevologic/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevologic/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevologic/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevologic/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevologic/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"publi